{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Wrapped up</b> — like a man who wraps the wind in his cloak so that he finds nothing, or <b>in her wings</b> in the wings of Beth Aven." "<b>And they shall be ashamed</b> — those who intercede." "<b>Their altars</b> — in Beth Aven."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The lemma צרר corresponds to the word in the verse rendered 'wrapped up'; Ibn Ezra reads it as a metaphor of gathering/wrapping something futile. The second alternative 'or in her wings' reflects the Hebrew reading בכנפיה as a variant or alternative parsing of the verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:14.358471813Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}